<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Fencing in Plano usually starts with one of three problems: a gray, leaning wood fence that has outlived its pickets, a section that came down in a spring storm, or a driveway gate that stopped opening. Many Plano subdivisions date from the 1980s to the 2000s, so a lot of backyards are on their second or third fence, and a lot of lots are alley-loaded with a gate or two to deal with.</p><p>White Rock Fence Co is advertising for independent fence contractors. It does not build, repair or install anything itself. Call <strong>(214) 555-0137</strong> and your request goes to an independent fence contractor who quotes the job in writing, and we suggest you get two or three comparable quotes before you pick one.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Plano</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Plano Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Wood privacy fence installation</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Replacing a worn 6-foot fence or stepping up to board-on-board with cedar pickets and steel posts. One DFW firm advertises installed cedar privacy fence at $18 to $28 per linear foot; another advertises $30 to $60 for 6-foot wood, so prices vary widely.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Fence repair after storms and age</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Leaning posts, missing pickets and wind-damaged sections. Plano's city handout says a permit is not required for repairs to an existing fence that do not exceed 25% of its area in a 12-month period.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Gate repair and automatic gates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Sagging walk gates, worn hinges, dead openers and sliding tracks. Power wiring for an opener is electrical work, so ask the installer who holds the electrical license.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Wrought iron and ornamental fences</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Iron or steel pickets for a front yard, where Plano wants fences under 40 inches and at least 50% open. One Dallas-area firm advertises residential tubular steel at $30 to $45 per linear foot installed.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
